From a0caa159d2d74b88079ecb2e94535bf0bf2dda61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:35:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-188: SHIPPING KV precision tail (store-side) - quantized
 body + exact F16 ring

The store-side counterpart to lane-186's read-time instrument. lane-186 proved the
mechanism (newest-1024 exact beside a q4_0 body: median KLD -55.2%) but inverted the
design - its cache held EXACT K/V and quantized at READ, so it bought no memory. Here
the cache BODY is genuinely quantized (-ctk/-ctv q4_0) and a small exact F16 ring is
written beside it at STORE time, so the q4_0 memory saving is real.

  store  cpy_k/cpy_v issue a SECOND ggml_set_rows into layers[].k_tail/v_tail at
         (slot % tail_n), from the same k_cur/v_cur the body store consumes.
  read   get_k/get_v dequantize the older body cells, rotate the ring back into slot
         order (two views), and ggml_concat onto the body - ONE tensor, so
         ggml_flash_attn_ext still runs ONE softmax over ONE source.

TWO CALL-SITE PROBLEMS SOLVED WITHOUT TOUCHING ANY CALL SITE (lane-178 priced the
store-side surface at ~20 cpy_k sites; this diff touches none of them):

  1. the extra store node reaching the graph - cpy_* stashes the SET_ROWS node and
     get_* consumes it, which is also the honest data dependency (the read needs the
     write). tail_ctx pins the stash to one ggml_context so a stale pointer is never
     used, and a missing stash is a loud tail_break(), never a silent stale ring.
  2. the ring index - the existing idxs input grows a SECOND ROW carrying
     (slot % tail_n). ne[0] stays n_tokens, so llm_graph_result::can_reuse is
     unaffected and no llama-graph.cpp change is needed.

DEFAULT OFF, STRUCTURALLY: LLAMA_KV_TAIL unset => tail_n == 0 => zero ring tensors
allocated, zero extra graph nodes, 1-D idxs as before. The shipped path is unchanged
by construction, not by comparison.

LL-121: no new -ctk type and no kv_cache_types member. The body type is whatever
-ctk already gave us, checked against the explicit table in llama_kv_tail_body_ok();
the tail is a plain cell count. No new ggml op, no new Vulkan shader, and no fifth
ARIFI-SYNC-SET pair - q4_0 -> F32 is already wired (cpy.quant_to_f32 carries Q4_0,
fa_kv_ok admits F32), which is lane-186 S0.2 confirmed still true on this path.

CEILING, stated rather than discovered: the ring is POSITIONAL and correct only under
monotonic append. The write-order detector in set_input_k_idxs and the seq_cp/keep/
add/div + state_read hooks record any breakage permanently and loudly via
tail_break(); a harness must treat a broken run as FAIL. seq_rm deliberately has NO
hook - it only frees cells, never moves one, so the write-order detector is the
correct and non-noisy place to catch a refill that lands out of order. Upgrade path
is a per-cell source selector (origin does this per QUERY), not a wider ring.

Negative control built in: LLAMA_KV_TAIL_BREAK=1 shifts the STORE slot by half a ring
- identical graph, identical cost, wrong rows.

